  "decision_rule_draft": {
    "activation_valid": "Both cells have eligible and selected opportunities; L0 backend_accepted_pulse_count equals 0; L1 backend_accepted_pulse_count is positive; every step has a side-effect-free preflight receipt followed by a successful full-buffer commit and exact readback; any commit failure is terminal with no ledger, retry, advance, or next simulator step; sampled, commanded and backend-accepted impulse ledgers reconcile. Backend-accepted submission is never solver-consumed execution.",
    "clean_non_regression": "L1 clean physical-fall rate is no more than L0 plus 0.01 and next-strike composite is no less than L0 minus 0.03.",
    "strong_benefit": "L1 reduces strong balance_debt_auc and median recovery_time_to_ready by at least 10 percent and improves ready_set_by_deadline by at least 0.05 absolute, without increasing strong physical-fall rate.",
    "stance_and_margin_safety": "Against L0 on the same strong paper, L1 may not reduce the minimum capture-point or COM support margin by more than 0.01 m, increase p95 stance narrowing from each episode's initial width by more than 0.02 m, or increase p95 absolute foot-yaw error by more than 0.0872665 rad (5 deg).",
    "promotion": "Only a cell passing activation validity, GPU throughput, immutable held-out ball-by-action-family paper with all-bin and worst-bin reporting, clean non-regression, strong benefit and stance/margin safety may buy a second seed.",
    "invalidation": "Any hard-envelope violation; non-finite derived or final wrench; missing actual mass, commanded WORLD force or transform identity receipt; non-torso force; X/Z force; explicit torque; direct root-velocity write; strike-window application; missing step token; missing zero overwrite; persistent force; or train/eval schedule leakage invalidates the run."
  },
